/// `parallel-checking`: the checker runs the checks of a readmission on its
/// pool, and forks the obligations of a long drain.
///
/// Implemented: `gandr check` forks the last drain of a declaration on its pool.
/// It forks a drain only when the drain holds 64 code obligations or more.
/// Each run holds 16 obligations or more, and each thread takes one run.
/// The driver installs the fork only in a run of fewer sources than threads.
/// The forked drain gives the verdict of the serial drain.
///
/// A check on more than one thread runs the checks of each readmission on its
/// pool. The calling thread releases each declaration in module order. A
/// worker runs each check. A declaration that names a running declaration
/// waits for the running checks. Each check gives the verdict of the serial
/// check.
///
/// Not implemented: no fork splits the arguments of an application.
/// No fork splits the branches of a case.
/// A run of as many sources as threads or more does not fork a drain.
/// No edge of the schedule names the declarations that a check reads.
/// No check starts on predicted entries.
///
/// - owes: #2802 — the forks at the frames of a check
/// - owes: #3476 — the checks that start on predicted entries
/// - owes: #7020 — the collision edges of the schedule

// `cylinderComposite2`.
import std.math.cylinder (cylinderComposite2);

/// Two squares of paths side by side, at identity verticals. The check of
/// this source readmits `std.math.cylinder`. On more than one thread, its
/// checks run on the pool. Its composites hold last drains of 64 obligations
/// or more. A check on more than one thread forks them.
def sideBySide(
  A : Type,
  x : A,
  y : A,
  z : A,
  f0 : Path[.A = A](x, y),
  f1 : Path(x, y),
  a : Path[.A = Path[.A = A](x, y)](f0, f1),
  g0 : Path(y, z),
  g1 : Path(y, z),
  b : Path[.A = Path[.A = A](y, z)](g0, g1)
) -> Path[.A = Path[.A = A](x, z)](Path.step f0 g0, Path.step f1 g1) =
  cylinderComposite2 A x y f0 x y f1 (Path.here x) (Path.here y) a z g0 z g1 (Path.here z) b
